     %%%    L o o p m a r k   L e g e n d    %%%

     Primary Loop Type        Modifiers
     ------- ---- ----        ---------
     A - Pattern matched      a - atomic memory operation
                              b - blocked
     C - Collapsed            c - conditional and/or computed
     D - Deleted               
     E - Cloned               f - fused
     G - Accelerated          g - partitioned
     I - Inlined              i - interchanged
     M - Multithreaded        m - partitioned
                              n - non-blocking remote transfer
                              p - partial
                              r - unrolled
                              s - shortloop
     V - Vectorized           w - unwound


    1.               SUBROUTINE XGETUA(IUNITA,N)
    2.         C***BEGIN PROLOGUE  XGETUA
    3.         C***DATE WRITTEN   790801   (YYMMDD)
    4.         C***REVISION DATE  820801   (YYMMDD)
    5.         C***CATEGORY NO.  R3C
    6.         C***KEYWORDS  ERROR,XERROR PACKAGE
    7.         C***AUTHOR  JONES, R. E., (SNLA)
    8.         C***PURPOSE  Returns unit number(s) to which error messages are being
    9.         C            sent.
   10.         C***DESCRIPTION
   11.         C     Abstract
   12.         C        XGETUA may be called to determine the unit number or numbers
   13.         C        to which error messages are being sent.
   14.         C        These unit numbers may have been set by a call to XSETUN,
   15.         C        or a call to XSETUA, or may be a default value.
   16.         C
   17.         C     Description of Parameters
   18.         C      --Output--
   19.         C        IUNIT - an array of one to five unit numbers, depending
   20.         C                on the value of N.  A value of zero refers to the
   21.         C                default unit, as defined by the I1MACH machine
   22.         C                constant routine.  Only IUNIT(1),...,IUNIT(N) are
   23.         C                defined by XGETUA.  The values of IUNIT(N+1),...,
   24.         C                IUNIT(5) are not defined (for N .LT. 5) or altered
   25.         C                in any way by XGETUA.
   26.         C        N     - the number of units to which copies of the
   27.         C                error messages are being sent.  N will be in the
   28.         C                range from 1 to 5.
   29.         C
   30.         C     Latest revision ---  19 MAR 1980
   31.         C     Written by Ron Jones, with SLATEC Common Math Library Subcommittee
   32.         C***REFERENCES  JONES R.E., KAHANER D.K., "XERROR, THE SLATEC ERROR-
   33.         C                 HANDLING PACKAGE", SAND82-0800, SANDIA LABORATORIES,
   34.         C                 1982.
   35.         C***ROUTINES CALLED  J4SAVE
   36.         C***END PROLOGUE  XGETUA
   37.               DIMENSION IUNITA(5)
   38.         C***FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  XGETUA
   39.  I            N = J4SAVE(5,0,.FALSE.)
   40.  V----<       DO 30 I=1,N
   41.  V               INDEX = I+4
   42.  V               IF (I.EQ.1) INDEX = 3
   43.  V  I            IUNITA(I) = J4SAVE(INDEX,0,.FALSE.)
   44.  V---->    30 CONTINUE
   45.               RETURN
   46.               END

